# The hero's crouch, completing a mirror that was half-named.
#
# armed_poses.map named HERO_CROUCH_LEFT from CAVES's crouch routines but
# left the right-facing side alone. The two routines are exact mirrors, and
# reading them side by side shows what was missing:
#
#   HERO_CROUCH_DOWN_LEFT_STEP:      CV_17A8 -> HERO_CROUCH_LEFT (x2)
#   HERO_CROUCH_DOWN_RIGHT_STEP:     CV_1600 -> CV_61B0          (x2)
#   HERO_CROUCH_HOLD_LEFT_LOOP:      HERO_CROUCH_LEFT, HERO_STAND_ARMED_LEFT
#   HERO_CROUCH_HOLD_RIGHT_LOOP:     CV_61B0,          HERO_STAND_ARMED_RIGHT
#
# So CV_61B0 occupies, on the right, exactly the position HERO_CROUCH_LEFT
# occupies on the left -- in two different routines -- and CV_17A8 / CV_1600
# are the transition frame each STEP routine draws before settling.
#
# The heights confirm the reading without reference to any name. Each
# direction descends through the same three stages:
#
#   left    45.0 stand armed  ->  38.0 crouching down  ->  33.0 crouched
#   right   44.5 stand armed  ->  37.5 crouching down  ->  32.5 crouched
#
# all at 11 leaves, all drawn at [HERO_X]. CV_61B0 has one other draw at a
# literal x=297, which reuses the pose rather than contradicting it.
CV_17A8 HERO_CROUCH_DOWN_LEFT
CV_1600 HERO_CROUCH_DOWN_RIGHT
CV_61B0 HERO_CROUCH_RIGHT
